  "reasoning": "The defendant contracted a renovation project, received most of the payment, and then refused to pay the workers their earned wages, even fleeing to avoid payment. After the police case was opened, he eventually paid the owed wages. Under Chinese criminal law, the act of refusing to pay labor remuneration after having received payment for work performed constitutes the crime of ‘拒不支付劳动报酬罪’. No other criminal conduct (such as fraud or illegal possession) is clearly established, as the defendant eventually paid the wages and there is no indication of intent to permanently deprive the workers of their remuneration. Therefore, the appropriate charge is ‘拒不支付劳动报酬’.",
